A host gives the event loop a turn before each extension's import and each
factory.

A host runs every conversation on one thread, and each conversation loads
every extension its folder has. Importing an extension and running its
factory is mostly synchronous, and the load awaited only microtasks between
them, so a whole load held the thread while every other conversation
waited: on the soak's days 2 and 3, opening the conversations held it 1.0
to 2.0 s, and each of 20 reloads over 1 s.

Yield to the loop with setImmediate before each import and before each
factory, so the longest hold is one extension's import or one factory. The
extensions load in the same order, one at a time, as before.

Apply only to the host's private pi build; ordinary interactive pi stays
unchanged.

--- a/packages/coding-agent/src/core/extensions/loader.ts
+++ b/packages/coding-agent/src/core/extensions/loader.ts
@@ -766,6 +766,16 @@
 	return extension;
 }
 
+// pi-host: one host runs many conversations on one thread, and each loads every extension
+// its folder has. Importing one and running its factory is mostly synchronous, and awaiting
+// them yields only to microtasks, so on the soak's days 2 and 3 a host opening its
+// conversations held the thread 1.0 to 2.0 s, and each of 20 reloads over 1 s, while every other
+// conversation waited. Yield to the event loop before each import and each factory, so the
+// longest hold is one extension's import or one factory.
+function yieldToLoop(): Promise<void> {
+	return new Promise((resolve) => setImmediate(resolve));
+}
+
 async function loadExtension(
 	extensionPath: string,
 	cwd: string,
@@ -776,12 +786,14 @@
 	const resolvedPath = resolvePath(extensionPath, cwd, { normalizeUnicodeSpaces: true });
 
 	try {
+		await yieldToLoop();
 		const factory = await loadExtensionModule(resolvedPath, cacheToken);
 		time(`${extensionPath} module import`, "extensions");
 		if (!factory) {
 			return { extension: null, error: `Extension does not export a valid factory function: ${extensionPath}` };
 		}
 
+		await yieldToLoop();
 		const extension = await initializeExtension(factory, extensionPath, resolvedPath, cwd, eventBus, runtime);
 		Object.defineProperty(extension, madeBy, { value: factory });
 
